cheaper.
    In general, there can be an exponential number of minimal repairs. When we calculate the dual polynomial associated
to a sentence we should leave it in expression form rather than put it in polynomial form because the latter may have
exponential size. The expression can stay in polysize. When we solve the equation for repairs, the and-or tree of repairs
is also of polynomial size. (All this is data complexity.) Any minimal repair is a subset of a repair represented in the
tree.



7.3 Repairs by provenance polynomials

In a general sense, the method to compute (minimal) repairs is just a variation of the method computing updated
provenance polynomials described in Sect. 6. Assume that 𝔄 is a 𝜏-structure with universe A such that 𝔄 6 |= 𝜓. Assume
further that to repair 𝔄 and make it a model of 𝜓, we have sets 𝑅 − and 𝑅 + of facts that we are allowed to remove from
or add to 𝔄.
     As in Sect. 6 we have a provenance-tracking model-defining interpretation 𝛽 : Lit 𝐴 (𝜏) → N[𝑋, 𝑋] which defines
the model 𝔄 𝛽 = 𝔄 and tracks the facts in 𝑅 + ∪ 𝑅 − that can potentially be added to or deleted from 𝔄.
     A repair for 𝔄 and 𝜓 is now an update 𝑅 ⊆ 𝑅 + ∪ 𝑅 − such that the modified structure 𝔄[𝑅] is a model for 𝜓.
     Let 𝑋 be the set of indeterminates 𝑥 𝛼 where 𝛼 ∈ 𝑅 + ∪ 𝑅 − . We again consider the model-compatible interpretation
𝜋 : Lit 𝐴 (𝜏) → N[𝑋, 𝑋] such that, for every atom 𝛼 ∈ 𝑅 + ∪ 𝑅 − , we have 𝜋(𝛼) = 𝑥 𝛼 and 𝜋(¬𝛼) = 𝑥 𝛼 , and all other
literals 𝛽 = 𝛼 or 𝛽 = ¬𝛼 where 𝛼 is not in 𝑅 + ∪ 𝑅 − (i.e. can not be changed) is simply mapped it to its truth value in 𝔄.
     We now consider the provenance polynomial 𝜋 [[𝜓]] ∈ N[𝑋, 𝑋] and the subset 𝑋 ± = {𝑥 𝛼 : 𝛼 ∈ 𝑅 + } ∪ {𝑥 𝛼 : 𝛼 ∈
   −
𝑅 } ⊆ 𝑋 ∪ 𝑋 of the dual indeterminates that are directly associated with the possible changes.
     We write 𝜋 [[𝜓]] = 𝑚 1 + · · · + 𝑚 𝑘 as a sum of monomials, and let 𝑣(𝑚) be the set of variables from 𝑋 ∪ 𝑋 appearing
in 𝑚. However, not all these variables are necessarily in 𝑋 ±, since 𝑋 ∪ 𝑋 also contains their duals. By examining what
combinations of indeterminates from 𝑋 ± occur in the monomials of 𝜋 [[𝜓]], we can read off all minimal repairs.
